#X text 1409 34 WESTERN_BGM_WITH_DRUMS.pd - simple cowboy/western background music with a drum groove for the ball rolling scene.;
#X text 1409 65 Algorithmic composition approach: vertical re-orchestration. Unity can add/remove layers with musicstate/danger values.;
#X text 1401 133 Click DSP_ON first. Use START/STOP to test without Unity.;
#X text 1414 183 Manual controls: START/STOP \, tempo buttons 90/110/130 BPM \, music state 0/1/2 \, and master volume.;
#X text 1414 503 Sequencer: a 16-step loop. Tempo is converted into an eighth-note step length using expr 30000 / BPM.;
#X text 1848 503 Layer 1: plucked western lead. A saw/phasor tone with a short envelope makes a simple guitar/banjo-like cowboy melody.;
#X text 1504 678 Layer 2: bass pulse. It turns on when musicstate >= 1 \, giving the scene more motion and weight.;
#X text 1999 863 Layer 3: noise percussion / horse-gallop rhythm. It turns on when musicstate >= 2 for a more intense riding feeling.;
#X text 2312 499 Layer 0: quiet E/B drone. This keeps the western scene grounded even when only the simple layer is active.;
#X text 2354 158 Master FX: high-pass + low-pass shaping \, one-tap echo \, soft clipping \, master volume \, then dac~.;
#X text 2353 108 Design goal: a simple American western/cowboy BGM that can grow from calm riding music into a more energetic chase feel.;
#X text 1386 1031 Layer 4: drum groove. Kick on strong beats \, snare on backbeats \, and a short high-noise shaker/hat pattern create a stronger western riding rhythm. This layer turns on when musicstate >= 1;
